    description: "Surfaced from WI-sukav investigation. alertmanager hg.json from deep-20260407-050552 contains a dispatches_to edge \\`URL.UnmarshalYAML → mailDev.UnmarshalYAML\\` (conf 0.30 — already test-downweighted per WI-supok). URL is in config/common/url.go and mailDev is in notify/email/email_test.go. They are in different packages with no inheritance, embedding, or interface relationship — only a coincidental shared method name (UnmarshalYAML, satisfying yaml.v2.Unmarshaler). The dispatches_to edge should have a yaml.v2.Unmarshaler interface as the source, not URL itself. This appears to be a cross-package short-name collision case distinct from the within-file embedding issue (the embedding case was the bulk of WI-sukav). Investigate type_hierarchy.py linker behavior when an interface has implementers in multiple packages — likely the issue is that URL is being incorrectly classified as a parent of mailDev via name lookup, possibly because of how _resolve_method_class_id handles ambiguity when multiple types share method names. This is the kind of issue PR #2721 addressed for cross-package class-ID collision; check whether that fix should extend to cover this dispatch direction too."  # a459
    fields: {}  # a459
